{"author":{"id":"7674679dac9170669f752d932f8b5955b1d55717359e13b1c1e687003c7bb99f"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1791436700,"nonce":"q+5G35xM7B5JudFq/OINhAyE4RE=","message":"Amended by doc/design/repoint.md, built on 2026-10-07 (67c23751, c4e29e07):\n\n- **Sweep first.** Every run, before any loser is consolidated, every relation naming a non-winner copy is re-pointed to the Index winner, archived or not. It writes under the shape check, and a refusal is that issue's own failed line. consolidate no longer re-points.\n- **Archive last.** The order is: sync the loser; fill the winner and add the note (once, keyed by jira-consolidated-from); then archive the loser. A failure part-way is retried by the next scan.\n- **The loser stamp.** The loser's create metadata carries jira-consolidated-into = winner, so map(select(.metadata[\"jira-consolidated-into\"] == null)) drops losers from a report.","files":null}]}